+<item>
+<title>Telegram macOS</title>
+<description>New:&lt;br&gt;• Create polls in Saved Messages.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Improved:&lt;br&gt;• Profile gift previews now animate smoothly back into their bubbles when closed.&lt;br&gt;• The message composer and rich-text editor remember your last target language for translation.&lt;br&gt;• Group admins can moderate a participant’s reactions from the reactions menu, with VoiceOver support.&lt;br&gt;• Telegram opens straight to your chats instead of showing an empty window first, and the chat list appears sooner&lt;br&gt;• Telegram uses much less memory while the AI agent is working: its activity animation no longer uses graphics memory&lt;br&gt;• Telegram uses less memory: cached images you aren't looking at no longer count toward its memory use, avatars and other generated images don't keep extra copies, multi-colour text takes half the memory, and the language pack is no longer kept twice&lt;br&gt;• The media viewer frees videos and pages you've moved past (up to about 40 MB less while browsing GIFs), resumes videos where you left off, and no longer prepares a player for every nearby video when it opens&lt;br&gt;• When Telegram is hidden or covered for a few minutes, it releases images and data it can quickly reload&lt;br&gt;• AI chats load at launch without slowing it down, and chats you aren't using free their memory&lt;br&gt;• Profile photo backgrounds, wallet cards and gift cut-outs no longer use extra graphics memory&lt;br&gt;• Gift backgrounds and wallet collectibles are freed soon after you close the screens that show them, and stickers no longer keep a decoded copy while visible&lt;br&gt;• The sticker and GIF panels free their memory when you haven't opened them for a few minutes and come back at the same place&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fixed:&lt;br&gt;• The Share window sends links, contacts, stories, QR codes, and comments to the selected forum topic.&lt;br&gt;• The media viewer stays on the same photo when new photos arrive.&lt;br&gt;• Public profile photos no longer show an incorrect date.&lt;br&gt;• Polls that allow new options keep Add Option available after you vote. Enabling anonymous voting turns off Add Option.&lt;br&gt;• Pressing Down in chat search no longer hangs when there are no recent chats. Return can open the top result after you change the search.&lt;br&gt;• Rich-message lists align their markers with the text and respect custom numbering. Nested media fits its column, and dividers are centered.&lt;br&gt;• Media slider previews in the rich-text editor keep spoilers covered. Plain-text copies put a quote and its author on separate lines.&lt;br&gt;• Copy Link no longer crashes after triple-clicking at the end of a line.&lt;br&gt;• Telegram could crash when closing a profile&lt;br&gt;</description>
+<pubDate>2026-18-11 04:29:58</pubDate>
